-function approach(){return `<div class="workspace prose"><div class="section-kicker">HOW BRIDGE WORKS</div><h1>Useful guidance.<br>Clear limits.</h1><p class="lead">One business challenge, a focused shortlist and a week to learn what works.</p><h2>A fit score is a starting point.</h2><p>We match documented task coverage, business type, your budget, named tools and setup effort. Your write-in description can identify a task or add context. These are transparent rules, not a prediction of business success. If the task is unclear or no suitable tool exists, we say so.</p><h2>Evidence belongs beside the recommendation.</h2><p>Every tool links to vendor documentation and pricing. A feature or connector listing does not verify a particular workflow. Current plan eligibility and usage costs need checking before you buy. Free-tier plans are explicit; unknown paid prices are never treated as zero.</p><h2>Time and cash tell different stories.</h2><p>Hours freed are your estimate, checked during a trial. An hourly value can describe the value of that time, but it is not cash saved. Cash savings need a named expense and a realistic reduction, capped at your reported spending. Net cash impact subtracts confirmed tool costs only.</p><h2>Your first week works without AI coaching.</h2><p>Survey, matches, comparisons and plans use catalog data and clear rules. The optional review only shows live advice after a successful live response. A missing connection leaves the plan usable. Sign-in, ongoing coaching and cross-device saving are next-phase work.</p><h2>Community claims need real data.</h2><p>This prototype does not collect or display community usage statistics. The design distinguishes adding a tool to a plan, actually trying it and choosing to keep it. Any future insights will need explicit opt-in and enough aggregated, real data to support the claim.</p>${btn('Find my fit '+arrow,'start')}</div>`;}
